course: dictionary
lesson: 2269
title: Creator and context
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A creator is a person who makes or invents something new, such as a story, game, character or video. The words around the word give clues: «Viral dances are made by real people, often young creators» tells you creators are the people who make the dances.
explain: A capital letter changes the meaning. The Creator means God, who Christians, Jews and Muslims believe made the world and everything in it. «Many Buddhists do not believe in a creator God» uses a small c, so it is about a maker in general, not the Creator of the religions.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. In «Copyright is a law that protects creators' work», if creator means the person who made something, the sentence still makes sense: the law protects the work of the people who made it.
fact: A creator is a person who makes or invents something new.
fact: «The Creator», with a capital C, means God in religion.
fact: Christians, Jews and Muslims believe God made the world and everything in it.
fact: A content creator makes videos, games or posts for other people to see online.
fact: An apostrophe after the s, as in «creators' work», shows that the work belongs to several creators.
exercise: «Viral dances are made by real people, often young creators.» What does creator mean here? | A fast kind of car | * A person who makes something new | A place where dances are sold
exercise: In religion, what does «the Creator» mean? | * God, who Christians, Jews and Muslims believe made the world | A famous painter from long ago | A shop that sells pictures | A kind of holiday
exercise: Find and copy one word from «Copyright is a law that protects creators' work». | law | copyright | work | * creators'
test: What is a content creator? | Someone who copies other people's dances | * Someone who makes videos, games or posts for others to see online | A teacher who marks homework | A person who sells old books
test: In «an inordinate fondness for beetles», what does inordinate mean? | Very small | Not at all | Quite a little | * Far more than anything else
exam: Why is it fair to name the creator when you copy their dance? | Because it makes the dance longer | Because the creator is always a teacher | * Because it gives credit to the person who made it
